# HOPPER CI FAILURE DIAGNOSIS & SDLC ENGINE CONFIGURATION
# ==============================================================================

# Node Environment & App
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3000
APP_NAME=Hopper
APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# GitHub App Authentication
I would judge its work against these three things:
1. One-command application startup
Required

npm run dev


Frontend, backend and worker start together, with infrastructure readiness checked.

2. Production-parity testing
Required

npm run build
npm run start:local


Tests the actual compiled application, not just the Vite development server.

3. Reliable shutdown
Required

npm run stop
npm run infra:down


Stops processes without deleting your database or Redis data.
